WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.943 --> 00:00:08.919 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Welcome to South America episode one of three. First, I clear the chosen names
for a fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:09.569 --> 00:00:19.763 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
We begin in the north of South America: Colombia on the Caribbean, Venezuela
beside it, and the two small Guianas on the Atlantic, Guyana and Suriname.

3
00:00:20.433 --> 00:00:23.974 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Colombia and its neighbours into view.

4
00:00:26.491 --> 00:00:37.497 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Colombia sits in the north-west of South America on the Caribbean coast, with
Panama to its north, Venezuela to its east and Ecuador to its south.

5
00:00:38.149 --> 00:00:55.537 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
It is named for Christopher Columbus, who never set foot there. It has more
species of birds than any other country, and Gabriel García Márquez set One
Hundred Years of Solitude in a town modelled on his native Aracataca.

6
00:00:56.194 --> 00:01:06.724 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Colombia as the north-west corner of the continent: named for a
navigator who never visited it, and home to more bird species than anywhere
else on Earth.

7
00:01:07.407 --> 00:01:10.820 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Venezuela and its neighbours into view.

8
00:01:13.037 --> 00:01:25.657 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Venezuela faces the Caribbean to the north, with Colombia to its west, Brazil
to its south and Guyana to its east. The Orinoco river sweeps across the south
of the country.

9
00:01:26.312 --> 00:01:44.672 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Its name means "Little Venice", for the houses on stilts the first explorers
saw on Lake Maracaibo. Angel Falls, the highest waterfall in the world, drops
979 metres, and the country holds the largest proven oil reserves in the
world.

10
00:01:45.323 --> 00:01:53.589 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Venezuela as the country whose name means Little Venice, with the
world's highest waterfall dropping out of the jungle in its south.

11
00:01:54.269 --> 00:01:57.682 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Guyana and its neighbours into view.

12
00:01:59.888 --> 00:02:08.282 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Guyana lies on the Atlantic between Venezuela to its west and Suriname to its
east, with Brazil inland to the south.

13
00:02:08.939 --> 00:02:26.471 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Its name comes from an Amerindian word often read as "land of many waters". It
is the only country in South America whose official language is English, and
Kaieteur Falls drops more than four times as far as Niagara in a single fall.

14
00:02:27.134 --> 00:02:37.792 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Guyana as the English-speaking country on the Atlantic, named for its
many waters, with one of the world's great single-drop waterfalls.

15
00:02:38.484 --> 00:02:41.503 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Suriname and its neighbours into view.

16
00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:56.035 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Suriname is the smallest country in South America, on the Atlantic between
Guyana to its west and French Guiana to its east, with Brazil inland to the
south.

17
00:02:56.695 --> 00:03:18.079 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
It is named for the Suriname river, perhaps after the Surinen, its early
inhabitants. In 1667 the Dutch kept it in a peace with England that left
England New Amsterdam, now New York. Forest covers more than nine tenths of
the country, one of the highest shares in the world.

18
00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:30.840 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Suriname as the smallest country of South America and one of the most
forested, tied to the 1667 swap that gave England New York.

19
00:03:34.739 --> 00:03:45.780 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Colombia sits in the north-west with Venezuela to its east. Guyana and
Suriname follow along the Atlantic, with Brazil inland behind them.

20
00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:59.309 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember a navigator who never visited his namesake country, Little Venice,
the land of many waters, and the 1667 peace that gave England New York.
